SURFACE PARITY — what was ported from the web source (no scope narrowing)
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
The web `RequiresAuth` is an auth-gated section WRAPPER (it takes children), not a leaf.
Faithfully reproduced:
- Render ladder (RequiresAuth.tsx):
    * isLoading || !data            -> render the notice, NOT the children (the loading
                                       policy: never flash-then-hide children + tear down
                                       their in-flight queries). Native `.loading`.
    * mode==='forward_auth' &&
      capabilities[capability]       -> render children unchanged (no wrapper chrome).
                                       Native `.authorized`.
    * open mode / capability off     -> the provider-aware notice (the friendly empty
                                       state). Native `.gated`.
  PLUS the sanctioned P4-leaf `.error(msg)` branch (contract fetch failed before first
  resolve -> retry affordance; children still never mount, so the web "safe default"
  is preserved).
- Capability matrix: step_up_reauth / totp_enrollment / session_list / impersonation /
  rbac — wire (snake_case) raw values kept in lock-step with internal/api.AuthModeCapabilities;
  total `subscript` so a new key fails the compile (the web keyed-type safety).
- Stable selector: `requires-auth-empty-{capability}` (web `requiresAuthEmptyTestId`),
  applied via `.accessibilityIdentifier`; exported as a free function (web parity).
- Vendor-neutral copy: `provider_hint` rendered verbatim when present
  (requiresAuth.bodyWithHint), else the generic Authentik/Authelia/oauth2-proxy/Keycloak
  list (requiresAuth.body); title requiresAuth.title — all `{{feature}}`/`{{provider}}`
  interpolations ported to positional %@ / %1$@ / %2$@.
- Per-capability feature names (requiresAuth.featureName.*) ported verbatim.
- role="status": the notice is one combined VoiceOver element (title + body); the lock
  glyph is accessibilityHidden (web aria-hidden).
- P4-leaf live-state axis (orthogonal): live/stale/offline freshness chip + banner on the
  notice, with a one-shot auto-refresh on the stale transition (offline never refreshes).
- Data bound via the P1/S8 state-holder seam (RequiresAuthSource); the view issues no HTTP.
- i18n 100% via the P1/S10 facade (RequiresAuthStrings, table "RequiresAuth"); zero English
  literals in Swift beyond the web-default fallbacks.
- Telemetry: P1/S11 `view.opened` emitted exactly once with slug "RequiresAuth".
- a11y: VoiceOver labels on every interactive element (refresh, retry), Dynamic Type via
  Font.TS roles, Reduce-Motion-aware fade-in + skeleton shimmer (shared TSFadeIn/TSSkeleton).

